Overview of the Game
Provide a clear description of how the game works.  
The game plays as follows:
-	The player is introduced to The Gang (Shaggy, Scooby, Velma, Daphne, and Fred)
-	He is then given a brief introduction to the story
-	The Dean of Engineering hired the Scooby Gang to solve the paranormal case of the missing computers.
-	The Gang engages in a non-playable cutscene with banter
-	The Van arrives at The Street in front of ESB and gets introduced to the Villains (Ali Reza and Omar Arif)
-	 Reintroduce the task to the player, explain the controls, and ensure the phone sensors work
-	The player then enters ESB and is allowed free reign to the floor
-	There are two floors with only the first floor accessible for clue-gathering which unlocks the second floor and the secret lair
-	The floor has two classrooms, one bathroom, and a laboratory
-	There are 4 clues in total in the rooms and 6 accessible by talking to The Gang and NPCs
-	Picking up the clues requires the player to activate the search function and then proceed to use the Accelerometer (The clues in the bathroom require the flashlight to be turned on as well)
-	As the player gathers clues the progress bar increases and when all 10 are collected a notification will appear for the player that a new floor has been unlocked
-	The player then is allowed to use the elevator to go upstairs and confront the villains
-	The villains then down their costumes and scare the player and The Gang
-	The group flees and lure them outside into the street to be caught by the Police who were called by Velma
We as a group think because how straightforward yet entertaining the game is allows the user/player to enjoy the mystery and nostalgia.
